config BR2_PACKAGE_SQLITE2
	bool "sqlite2 (legacy)"
	select BR2_PACKAGE_READLINE
	select BR2_PACKAGE_NCURSES
	help
	  SQLite 2.8.17 - the last SQLite 2.x release (2005).

	  This is NOT a replacement for the "sqlite" package (which is
	  SQLite 3): the two are on-disk- and API-incompatible and install
	  side by side (libsqlite.so.0 + sqlite.pc vs libsqlite3.so.0 +
	  sqlite3.pc), so both can be enabled at once.

	  It exists here only because the GPE PIM stack (libgpepimc,
	  libtododb, gpe-sketchbook) is hard-wired to the sqlite 2 C API
	  (sqlite_open/sqlite_exec_printf/...), which was removed in
	  SQLite 3. Do not use it for anything new - it is unmaintained
	  and has no upstream security support.

	  https://www.sqlite.org/
